  "design_review": {
    "cycle": 70,
    "scope": "Pending ColumnTile lookup only; original maps, cells, generation, ordering and retirement remain authoritative.",
    "checks": [
      "Full (root, chunk X, chunk Z) equality after hashing; colliding slots always use the original map result.",
      "Cached Arcs borrow existing tiles; column_cell and original OnceLock<Result<Arc<ColumnState>>> still choose/build each state once.",
      "No user callback or recursive generation runs inside a map lock or cache initializer; publish the tile before invoking callback.",
      "Concurrent misses load the original map before competing to fill a slot; equal keys therefore share the original tile.",
      "Root completion requires mutable access after joined target evaluation; all extra cache owners clear before original pending.take. Array storage is reused.",
      "Error cleanup clears additional owners then delegates to original poison-recovering into_entries; normal sorted boundary retirement retained.",
      "Warm-cache poison observes the actual authoritative shard flag and attempts its original lock; same original error propagation. Concurrent poisoning remains visible at joined root take.",
      "Fixed 16,384 slots bound cached references regardless of coordinate reach. No dependency truncation or global cross-profile lifetime.",
      "Existing cfg(test) lookup observer now measures only actual original map loads. Full read cost, cache hit checks and clearing remain in complete-region wall time.",
      "Four targeted tests exercise key/root distinction, collisions, coordinate extremes, concurrent fill, nested same-shard callbacks, root reset, poison and ownership release.",
      "C69 held FirstError production code excluded; this candidate starts from accepted C68."
